    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48151" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thēricles</span></b> , is,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θηρικλῆς,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a famous potter of
				Grecian antiquity</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				40, 76, § 205</span></i> (from Theophr. Hist. Plant. 5,
			4).—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thēriclēus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-īus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Thericles</i>, <i>Thericlean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pocula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 18, § 38</span></i>
			.</div>
